{
  "_comment": "P4.D209 \u2014 the Scriptorium repo layer's WRITE-METADATA contract, driven through v4's REAL DocMountFileLinksRepository / DocMountBlobsRepository rather than through writeDatabaseDocument. That distinction is the whole instrument: writeDatabaseDocument re-chunks immediately, so it puts chunkCount straight back and bug 156 leaves no trace in a final-state dump. Calling linkDocumentContent directly is what every byte-preserving writer does, and it is where the defect lives. (1-6) bug 155 \u2014 an overwrite that says nothing about description / extractedText / extractionStatus must KEEP them; an explicit '' still clears; a fresh insert defaults blank; an explicit null clears where an omission keeps. (7-18) bug 156 \u2014 a repoint drops the old chunks and zeroes chunkCount, an unchanged rewrite leaves both alone, and a bound hard-link sibling is retired with the writer. (19-26) the per-location timestamps \u2014 lastModified + createdAt honoured on insert, lastModified alone on update leaving createdAt, the same on a blob write, `now` with no opinion, setLinkTimestamps moving lastModified on one path and createdAt on another (never on dated/doc.md, whose createdAt must reach the dump still carrying the value its INSERT was given \u2014 a later set would be indistinguishable from a blank-then-set), false for an unknown link and false for an empty ask. (27-33) bug 157 \u2014 one blob at TWO locations: each path resolves to its OWN link id, a caption lands on the asked path and leaves the twin blank, the two locations carry different captions, and extracted text is per location. The needs-rechunk probe is the rescan's own predicate (chunkCount == 0 || conversionStatus != 'converted') read back over every link.",
  "testPepperBase64": "ZpjI5jcj5CYsyBA6zPH90G4frQEbv2WsAhERvEKrjJk=",
